    "https://www.wvwc.edu/jobs/graduate-assistant-for-sports-information/": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant for Sports Information – West Virginia Wesleyan College",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant for Sports Information – West Virginia Wesleyan College Skip to content Home Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Visit Affordability International Transfer Commit to WVWC Financial Aid & Scholarships Students Academic Calendar Support Campus Life Community Engagement Student Accounts About About WVWC Campus Offices Conferences, Events, and Camps Consumer Information Contact Jobs News Academics Undergraduate Majors Graduate Programs Registrar Resources Alumni Athletics Give Home Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Visit Affordability International Transfer Commit to WVWC Financial Aid & Scholarships Students Academic Calendar Support Campus Life Community Engagement Student Accounts About About WVWC Campus Offices Conferences, Events, and Camps Consumer Information Contact Jobs News Academics Undergraduate Majors Graduate Programs Registrar Resources Alumni Athletics Give 59 College Ave. Buckhannon, WV 26201 (304)-473-8000 Admissions Housing About Students Alumni Give Contact 59 College Ave.         Buckhannon, WV 26201 (304)-473-8000 about Job Listings Graduate Assistant for Sports Information POSITION: Part-Time DATE POSTED: 2026-07-12 07:45:00 West Virginia Wesleyan College is seeking one (1) individual for the position of Graduate Assistant for Sports Information. A member of NCAA Division II and the Mountain East Conference, West Virginia Wesleyan College sponsors 22 intercollegiate sports. The Sports Information Graduate Assistant (GA) position is a 10-month graduate assistant position beginning August 1, 2026 and reports to the Sports Information Director. The GA will assist the Sports Information Department in the management of rosters, schedules, statistics, story writing and online media content creation for all 22 West Virginia Wesleyan Athletics programs. The GA will assist with gameday duties to prepare, conduct and recap home athletic events. The individual in this position will work twenty hours per week and must remain as a full-time student in good academic standing. Successful candidates must be accepted into one of West Virginia Wesleyan College’s graduate programs. The Sports Information GA will be an integral member of the WVWC Athletics Department regarding the planning and implementation of athletics content to engage supporters and promote teams and athletes. Additionally, this position will assist the department of compliance, and perform relevant duties regarding game operations and general athletics office support. Position Responsibilities: Assist in the management of rosters, schedules, and statistics for all 22 Athletics programs through the NCAA, the Mountain East Conference and the Bobcats website: com Write previews, recaps, and personal interest stories for the Bobcats website and other local, regional and national media. Assist in the creation and management of all West Virginia Wesleyan Athletics media, including photography, graphics, and video. Assist in the production of live broadcasts for all home competitions. Use social media platforms to enhance the reach of content, and engagement. Report to the Sports Information Director to assist in the planning and execution of Athletics events. Assist Compliance and Athletics Office upon request and other duties as assigned. Position Requirements and Preferred Experience: Bachelor’s degree in a related field (Sports Management, Communications, Business Administration, Marketing) Acceptance into one of WVWC’s graduate programs: https://www.wvwc.edu/graduate-programs/ Excellent written and interpersonal communication skills Strong journalistic writing ability and knowledge of AP style Proficiency in media creation software such as Photoshop, Canva or Box Out Sports. Wesleyan uses Box Out for the creation of social media posts. Experience with NCAA LiveStats (Genius Sports) software Broadcasting experience (play-by-play or color commentary) Diligent and organized working habits Position Benefits : Graduate Assistants will receive: Full tuition On Campus Housing Campus meal plan 10-month stipend To Apply: Review of applicants will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Candidates must submit the following electronically – letter of application, resume, portfolio (as applicable), and two references with contact information to Sports Information Director, Rigel Wilson at sportsinfo@wvwc.edu. Please enter “ your last name -Sports Information GA” on the subject line of the email. Located in Buckhannon, W.Va., West Virginia Wesleyan features a beautiful 100-acre campus of red-brick Georgian architecture. West Virginia Wesleyan was also named one of the best colleges in the South by U.S. News & World Report. West Virginia Wesleyan College does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, creed, ancestry, marital/family status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, religion, age, disability or blindness, or any other characteristic protected by local, state or federal law , to include Title VI, Title VII, Title IX, Section 504, and the Age Discrimination Act, in the administration of its admission policies, scholarship and loan programs, educational programs, employment, athletic programs, co-curricular activities, or other College administered programs. WVWC’s nondiscrimination polices may be accessed at https://www.wvwc.edu/title-ix/ .   For inquiries about the application of these laws in WVWC’s programs activities or to file a report, contact the Title IX Coordinator at titleix@wvwc.edu or 304-621-1316. About Wesleyan Contact Current Livestream Events Title IX Consumer Info Non-Discrimination Statement Privacy Library Shop News Potential Students Request Info Virtual Tour Visit Current Students Bobcat Connect eCampus Bookstore Blackboard Academic Support Academic Calendar Jobs Self-Service Self-Service Alumni Give ABU Resources Bobcat Beacon West Virginia Wesleyan College 59 College Ave. Buckhannon, WV 26201 (304)-473-8000"
    },
    "https://www.wvwc.edu/jobs/assistant-director-of-institutional-research/": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Institutional Research – West Virginia Wesleyan College",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Institutional Research – West Virginia Wesleyan College Skip to content Home Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Visit Affordability International Transfer Commit to WVWC Financial Aid & Scholarships Students Academic Calendar Support Campus Life Community Engagement Student Accounts About About WVWC Campus Offices Conferences, Events, and Camps Consumer Information Contact Jobs News Academics Undergraduate Majors Graduate Programs Registrar Resources Alumni Athletics Give Home Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Visit Affordability International Transfer Commit to WVWC Financial Aid & Scholarships Students Academic Calendar Support Campus Life Community Engagement Student Accounts About About WVWC Campus Offices Conferences, Events, and Camps Consumer Information Contact Jobs News Academics Undergraduate Majors Graduate Programs Registrar Resources Alumni Athletics Give 59 College Ave. Buckhannon, WV 26201 (304)-473-8000 Admissions Housing About Students Alumni Give Contact 59 College Ave.         Buckhannon, WV 26201 (304)-473-8000 about Job Listings Assistant Director of Institutional Research POSITION: Full-Time DATE POSTED: 2026-06-01 07:30:06 West Virginia Wesleyan College invites applications for a full-time Assistant Director of Institutional Research. The Assistant Director supports the collection, organization, analysis, and communication of institutional data for planning, accreditation, assessment, and strategic initiatives. The successful candidate will report to the Director and work closely with campus partners across Academic Affairs, Enrollment Management, Student Affairs, and Finance. Key responsibilities Assist with recurring internal reports, including enrollment and retention snapshots, course and credit hour summaries, and end-of-term reporting. Support preparation and submission of external reports and surveys (e.g., IPEDS, state reporting, accreditor requests, college guidebook surveys). Provide data and reporting support to academic and administrative units for assessment, program review, and planning. Help maintain and update institutional dashboards and data tools, including documentation of data definitions and basic data visualizations. Conduct ad hoc queries and descriptive analyses to inform operational and student success initiatives. Assist with the design, administration, and analysis of campus surveys (students, alumni, faculty, staff) and prepare concise summaries of results. Contribute to data quality checks, documentation, and data governance conversations. Qualifications Required Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field (e.g., higher education, social sciences, business, mathematics, statistics, data analytics, or related discipline). Experience working with data in a professional, internship, graduate assistantship, or substantial project context. Proficiency with spreadsheets (Excel or Google Sheets) for data cleaning, basic analysis, and visualization (e.g., charts, pivot tables). Strong attention to detail, organizational skills, and ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines. Clear written and oral communication skills, including the ability to explain data findings to non-technical audiences. Demonstrated discretion and professionalism in handling sensitive or confidential information. Preferred Experience working with a student information system or other administrative databases in higher education. Familiarity with basic query or reporting tools (e.g., SQL, MS Access, Argos, Tableau, Power BI, or similar). Exposure to institutional research, assessment, accreditation, or program evaluation in a college/university setting. Founded in 1890, West Virginia Wesleyan is a private residential college located in the foothills of the Appalachians in Buckhannon, WV, named one of the “100 Best Small Towns in America.” The College is related to the United Methodist Church, with a curriculum committed to intellectual rigor, self-discovery, human dignity, mutual support, social justice, self-discipline, mental and physical wellness, the appreciation of diversity and the natural world, and the judicious use of resources. The College has over 40 undergraduate academic majors, six graduate programs, 22 NCAA Division II sports, comprehensive student life, community engagement, and outdoor recreational programs. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Salary is commensurate with education and experience. To apply, e-mail a single PDF containing a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, and contact information for three references. Application materials should be sent to Dr. Lynn M. Linder, Provost & Executive Vice President for Academic Affairs at academicaffairs@wvwc.edu. Prior to a final offer of employment, the selected candidate will be required to submit to a background check. For questions about the position, please contact the Director of Institutional Research, Tammy Crites at crites_t@wvwc.edu. West Virginia Wesleyan College does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, creed, ancestry, marital/family status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, religion, age, disability or blindness, or any other characteristic protected by local, state or federal law , to include Title VI, Title VII, Title IX, Section 504, and the Age Discrimination Act, in the administration of its admission policies, scholarship and loan programs, educational programs, employment, athletic programs, co-curricular activities, or other College administered programs. WVWC’s nondiscrimination polices may be accessed at https://www.wvwc.edu/title-ix/. For inquiries about the application of these laws in WVWC’s programs activities or to file a report, contact the Title IX Coordinator at titleix@wvwc.edu or 304-621-1316. About Wesleyan Contact Current Livestream Events Title IX Consumer Info Non-Discrimination Statement Privacy Library Shop News Potential Students Request Info Virtual Tour Visit Current Students Bobcat Connect eCampus Bookstore Blackboard Academic Support Academic Calendar Jobs Self-Service Self-Service Alumni Give ABU Resources Bobcat Beacon West Virginia Wesleyan College 59 College Ave. Buckhannon, WV 26201 (304)-473-8000"
    },
    "https://www.wvwc.edu/jobs/custodian/": {
      "title": "Custodian – West Virginia Wesleyan College",
      "description": "Custodian – West Virginia Wesleyan College Skip to content Home Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Visit Affordability International Transfer Commit to WVWC Financial Aid & Scholarships Students Academic Calendar Support Campus Life Community Engagement Student Accounts About About WVWC Campus Offices Conferences, Events, and Camps Consumer Information Contact Jobs News Academics Undergraduate Majors Graduate Programs Registrar Resources Alumni Athletics Give Home Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Visit Affordability International Transfer Commit to WVWC Financial Aid & Scholarships Students Academic Calendar Support Campus Life Community Engagement Student Accounts About About WVWC Campus Offices Conferences, Events, and Camps Consumer Information Contact Jobs News Academics Undergraduate Majors Graduate Programs Registrar Resources Alumni Athletics Give 59 College Ave. Buckhannon, WV 26201 (304)-473-8000 Admissions Housing About Students Alumni Give Contact 59 College Ave.         Buckhannon, WV 26201 (304)-473-8000 about Job Listings Custodian POSITION: Full-Time DATE POSTED: 2026-04-23 20:18:16 West Virginia Wesleyan College is seeking a full-time, 12-month, Custodian. RESPONSIBILITIES OF POSITION: Perform housekeeping and cleaning of all facilities. The essential and marginal functions include: housekeeping of college facilities, performing set-up for special events, securing and unlocking buildings as required, inventory functions, and material requisition for supplies and any additional duties or job descriptions as assigned by administrative personal of West Virginia Wesleyan College. QUALIFICATION REQUIREMENTS: Ability to read, write, and understand oral and written communications. Working knowledge in the use of custodial equipment and power tools, i.e. buffers, burnishers, scrubbing unit, carpet equipment, etc. Must be knowledgeable of environmental products and their applications and disposal procedures. Must be able to climb step ladders. 1-year experience in the custodian trade (for new hire only). WORKING CONDITIONS: Requires ability to lift 25-50 lbs., climb ladders, twist bend knees, prolonged standing, sweeping and mopping, vacuuming, use power tools, and visually and manually inspect work being preformed on campus as needed. Exposure to cleaning products, dust, and dirt on a daily basis. Potential exposure to blood-borne pathogens. TERMS OF EMPLOYMENT: As determined by the Collective Bargaining Agreement and West Virginia Wesleyan College. EVALUATION: Performance of this position will be evaluated annually. TO APPLY: Interested candidates should submit a letter of interest, resume and names and contact information of three references to wvwcjobapp@wvwc.edu.  On the subject of the email, please enter:  ##7## – Custodian. The review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Equal Opportunity Policy West Virginia Wesleyan College is an equal opportunity employer. It is the policy of the College to create a favorable work environment in which all employees, regardless of race, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, disability, or religious affiliation, can enjoy equal opportunities in their employment relationship with the College. About Wesleyan Contact Current Livestream Events Title IX Consumer Info Non-Discrimination Statement Privacy Library Shop News Potential Students Request Info Virtual Tour Visit Current Students Bobcat Connect eCampus Bookstore Blackboard Academic Support Academic Calendar Jobs Self-Service Self-Service Alumni Give ABU Resources Bobcat Beacon West Virginia Wesleyan College 59 College Ave. Buckhannon, WV 26201 (304)-473-8000"
    },
